{# version: 1 #}
Write a peer review of a research paper in the style of an OpenReview review. Use only the
paper text below (every paragraph or table starts with an id in brackets) and the analysis
facts, which were established by checking the paper's tables, its reproducibility details
and its code. Be specific and fair; do not praise or criticise in general terms.

Return:
- "summary": 3-5 sentences on what the paper does and what it finds.
- "strengths": 2-5 points. Each point: "point" (one or two sentences), "quote" (ONE sentence
  copied character-for-character from the paper text that the point rests on) and
  "chunk_id" (the id in brackets of that paragraph).
- "weaknesses": 2-6 points, same shape. Use the analysis facts where they apply (a quote may
  then be ""). Do not invent problems the text and facts do not show.
- "missing_ablations": 0-4 experiments the paper's own claims would need but does not report,
  same shape (quote the claim they would support).
- "questions": 2-5 questions for the authors.
Do not give a score or an accept/reject recommendation. Do not compute anything.

Analysis facts:
{% for f in findings -%}
- [{{ f.source }}] {{ f.text }}
{% else -%}
(none)
{% endfor %}

Extracted overview:
{% for line in overview -%}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}

Paper text:
{{ text }}
